# Be - Ugur interatomic potential, hard truncation, the reference parameters
#
# pair_style ugur
# pair_coeff * * Be.ugur Be
#
# Truncation: hard - phi2 is cut at rcut2 and does NOT vanish there, so this set is for static properties, not dynamics
# MD: DO NOT USE.  At 600 K the crystal collapses: it reaches 308 K and its potential energy falls below the static lattice.  Static properties from this set are still valid.
#
# Nudge test: passed - displaced by 1e-5 A and relaxed, the lattice returns.
#
# Fitted to: cohesive energy, lattice constant, bulk modulus and the elastic
# constants of Be at its experimental lattice constant.  Nothing else.
#
# Format is LAMMPS's Tersoff convention - one line per ordered triple
# (centre, leg, leg) - so that this file and a multi-element one are read the
# same way.  For a single element that is one line.
#
# el1 el2 el3  m D alpha r0 gamma C alpha3 rcut2 rcut3 taper lam2 lam4
Be Be Be 6.4462987798146498 0.2034496432607753 0.39450431153032534 3.0330708913232103 0.49695848397503056 -0.082154775860638102 0.067996159168131218 5.9430800000000001 3.3379308558006988 -1 0 0
